WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.036
-Hello, everyone, and welcome
back to the attic crawl space.

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.904
On Monday,
we answered a question

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.940
many viewers had been
wondering about --

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.341
what's behind that tiny,
little door back there

00:00:09.341 --> 00:00:11.544
when my kids escaped at
the end of "Closer Look."

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:14.781
Now, a lot of people online
have said they were adorable

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.950
and too cute for words,
and I assure you,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.117
they are...

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:21.120
in nine-second chunks.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.088
Also, some of you might be
looking at me right now,

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:25.091
wondering, does Seth know
he's already worn that shirt?

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.760
And yeah, I know.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.328
I promise you, I know.

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:32.164
And I do wish I had
a deeper roster of shirts,

00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:35.034
but in my defense,
no one warned me

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:37.870
multiple times about
the possibility of a pandemic

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.005
because I'm not the president.

00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:41.207
That's a segue.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.942
And now, even after ignoring
those warnings,

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.612
the president is pushing to
prematurely reopen the economy,

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.380
threatening to repeat
the mistakes he made

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.148
at the start of this crisis.

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:51.818
For more of this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:55.488 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.257
When Donald Trump
was elected in 2016,

00:00:58.257 --> 00:01:01.293
this was exactly the kind
of nightmare scenario

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:02.328
everyone was afraid of --

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.397
What would happen
in a global crisis

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.965
if the most powerful
man in the world

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.700
was a racist game show host

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.702
who failed at virtually
everything in his life,

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:13.172
except for pretending to be
a successful businessman on TV?

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:15.408
and he is not even good
at pretending.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.343
Look at him pretending
to be president.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.312
He just stares directly
into the camera,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.713
and he can't even be bothered

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.782
to, at least, put some
fake documents on his desk.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.850
You can almost
hear the dial tone

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.652
blasting out of the phone.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:30.189
He looks like a tourist
taking a photo on the set

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:31.356
of "Deep Impact."

00:01:31.356 --> 00:01:32.391
[ As Donald Trump ] "Wow.

00:01:32.391 --> 00:01:35.094
Is this the phone
Morgan Freeman used?

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.362
You know, everyone freaked out

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.097
about the asteroid
in that movie,

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.899
but it ended up being no worse

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.735
than the common everyday flu."

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:43.902
[ Normal voice ] The point is,

00:01:43.902 --> 00:01:45.705
this is the crisis
everyone feared.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.773
In fact,
before Trump took office,

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:49.675
President Obama's outgoing team

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:51.744
tried to prepare
Trump's incoming team

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.279
for this exact scenario.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.948
a scenario experts
had warned about for years.

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:58.050
-Days before
Donald Trump took office,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.685
some
of President Obama's advisors

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.754
walked the incoming
president's team

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.222
through a hypothetical scenario

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:06.025
remarkably like the one
we are living through now.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.193
It was a briefing on what would

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:07.960
happen

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.829
if a quick spreading virus

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.831
were to race through
London and Seoul,

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.032
and in that scenario,
they presented governments

00:02:14.032 --> 00:02:15.401
imposing travel bans.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.536
There were shortages at
hospitals across the country,

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:18.972
and today,

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.740
roughly two-thirds of those
Trump administration officials

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.077
who participated
in that simulation

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.779
are no longer in government.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:27.780
-That's right.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.248
Most of the Trump officials

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:31.351
who worked for him back then
aren't even there anymore.

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.620
They're either in jail,
on Fox News,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.888
or in the bargain bin
at a Barnes &amp; Noble.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:36.655
"Hi, excuse me.

00:02:36.655 --> 00:02:38.157
This Sean Spicer book

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.592
only has blank pages."

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:42.461
"Huh, look at that.

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:45.598
I guess you're the first person
to ever open one."

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.667
This White House has
more staff turnover

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.670
than a Six Flags
over summer break.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.805
They made the Six Flags mascot

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.440
commerce secretary.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.575
What Obama's team
should have done is

00:02:56.575 --> 00:02:58.411
run a simulation
for what would happen

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.946
when a sociopath President
dismisses repeated warnings

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:03.382
from intelligence officials
and public health experts

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:04.850
that a pandemic is coming.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.985
and fires anyone
who's done any planning for it.

00:03:06.985 --> 00:03:09.555
Okay. So, the first thing
you do in that case is,

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.457
you call up Netflix,

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:12.859
and you get them to release

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.428
an emergency bonus episode
of "Tiger King" ASAP.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.929
You know, think of it as a --

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.864
I don't know --
a where-are-they-now situation.

00:03:18.864 --> 00:03:21.000
You know, maybe,
someone got new teeth.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.735
And, again, you know, obviously,

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.904
let's pray it never
comes to this.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:28.708
In fact, as we've now learned,
one former Trump official,

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.710
homeland security adviser
Tom Bossert was a part

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.879
of a group of people trying
to warn the government

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:37.149
in a series of exchanges
called the "Red Dawn" e-mails.

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:38.551
The e-mails were nicknamed

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.853
after the 1984
Patrick Swayze movie,

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.555
but, if you're going
to pick a Swayze movie,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.890
I feel like "Ghost" would
have been a better choice,

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:48.227
since the government's response
is clearly being lead by one.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:49.795
I mean, yikes.

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:51.196
[ Chuckles ] Look at him.

00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:53.899
Jared Kushner looks like
he just appeared out of nowhere

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:56.702
after someone read
an Edgar Allen Poe story

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:58.337
into a cracked mirror...

00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:00.907
and then demanded
you pay for the mirror.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.774
It's weird that
the public health response

00:04:02.774 --> 00:04:04.143
is being led by a guy

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.846
who looks like he would sneak
into your hospital room

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.248
and pinch your IV line closed

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:12.150
until you told him
where the microfilm was.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:15.888
"It's a simple question."

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.257
So, in those "Red Dawn" e-mails,

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.491
we found out
that Bossert and others

00:04:19.491 --> 00:04:21.060
had expressed concerns

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.062
about Trump's slow
and incoherent response,

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.164
like for example,
when trump announced

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:28.067
a hasty and confusing
European travel ban

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:31.003
that led to jam-packed airports
in cities like Chicago

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:33.539
after there were
already documented cases

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:36.108
of community spreading
here in the U.S.,

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:38.978
Bossert wrote,
"Can anyone justify

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:40.913
the European travel
restrictions,

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.048
scientifically?

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.249
Seriously, is there any benefit?

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:45.718
I don't see it,

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:48.020
but I'm hoping there's
something I don't know."

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.589
That's how we all feel,
but it's never the case.

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:52.925
With Trump, things are always
exactly as they seem.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:56.062
For example, we see him using
every muscle in his face

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.363
to squint at the teleprompter

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:58.897
like he is staring
at a "Magic Eye" poster

00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:01.100
and say, "I think
the president can't see,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.469
but I'm hoping there's
something I don't know."

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.671
And then, you tune in
to his unhinged

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:07.673
Rose Garden press conference
Tuesday night,

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:08.640
in which he announced,

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.376
in the middle of
a global pandemic,

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.712
that he was pulling funding
from World Health Organization,

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:14.647
and you see this.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.149
-I instructed my team to use

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:18.584
the Defense Protection Act.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:22.921
and the Defense Production Act

00:05:22.921 --> 00:05:26.292
was used very powerfully.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:30.296
All the aid that we send
will be...discussed...

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.297
at very, very powerful letl--

00:05:32.297 --> 00:05:33.098
letters.

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:34.267
We see light.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.235
We're starting to see it
more than ever before.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:40.940
We've held our...

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.541
rate, the numbers,

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:44.610
everything we've done.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.545
We've been very, very...

00:05:46.545 --> 00:05:48.648
strong on it
and very powerful on it.

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:50.582
-He sounds like
a guy on a date

00:05:50.582 --> 00:05:52.117
getting lines
through an earpiece

00:05:52.117 --> 00:05:53.819
and the feed just cut out.

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:57.122
[ As Donald Trump ] The light
in your eyes is so...

00:05:57.122 --> 00:05:58.958
It's so...

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.559
Well, it is lighty.

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:03.629
I mean, they're your eyes.
You know.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.299
[ Normal voice ] Also,
I like when his brain melts,

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:08.634
his go to-words
are strong and powerful.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.670
it's like I'm listening
to a focus group

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.571
